  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $316M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Agriculture made 2,567 awards with an average award size of $123K. Obligations fell 97.1% year over year. Historical annual totals show FY22 obligations of $10B, FY23 obligations of $11.5B, FY24 obligations of $11.6B, FY25 obligations of $9.6B, and FY26 obligations of $10.9B. The FY2027 to date total is concentrated in a few sectors, with Logging accounting for $99.6M and the next largest categories including Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $29.1M and Support Activities for Forestry at $28.8M. Top vendors in FY2027 to date include PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC with $99.6M, ARCHER-DANIELS-MIDLAND COMPANY with $14M, and BRANTLEY CONSTRUCTION SERVICES, LLC with $7.9M. The FY2027 to date picture shows a sharp step down from prior full fiscal years and a spend pattern focused on forestry and food-related industries alongside a mix of construction and IT services.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Department of Agriculture contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture's obligations fell 97.1% year over year. The Department of Agriculture obligated $316M in FY2027 to date compared with FY26 obligations of $10.9B and earlier years of $11.6B in FY24, $11.5B in FY23, and $10B in FY22. The FY2027 to date total is therefore a small share of recent full-year totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the leading procurement categories and vendors in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Logging is the largest category with $99.6M in obligations. The Department of Agriculture also obligated $29.1M for Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation, $28.8M for Support Activities for Forestry, and $25.5M for All Other Miscellaneous Food Manufacturing. Top vendors include PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC with $99.6M, ARCHER-DANIELS-MIDLAND COMPANY with $14M, and BRANTLEY CONSTRUCTION SERVICES, LLC with $7.9M."
      }
    ]
