  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Agriculture spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $316M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Agriculture made 2,567 awards with an average award size of $123K, and obligations fell 97.1% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years such as FY26 obligations of $10.9B."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Agriculture buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Agriculture buys a mix of forestry, food manufacturing, transportation, construction, and IT services in FY2027 to date. Logging accounts for $99.6M, Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation accounts for $29.1M, Support Activities for Forestry accounts for $28.8M, and All Other Miscellaneous Food Manufacturing accounts for $25.5M, among other categories."
    },
